# Reference pointers only: do NOT copy this file to root .env.
#
# PBX Compose variables:
#   cp freepbx/.env.example freepbx/.env
#   Edit freepbx/.env, then run Compose from freepbx/.
# Canonical instructions: docs/WINDOWS-PBX.md
# DB credentials are private file secrets under freepbx/secrets/, not variables
# in this root file. freepbx/prepare.py defaults to dry-run and never starts Docker.
#
# Bridge/profile credentials:
#   Follow docs/SETUP.md and scripts/setup.py generate --help.
#   Generation creates an independent private bundle with bridge.env and profile
#   secrets. ARI_USER and ARI_PASSWORD must match the PBX ARI user; do not create
#   a second mismatched password. DB/admin/SIP/API credentials are separate.
#   ARI URL/app and AudioSocket addresses are YAML settings, not env overrides.
#
# Never commit .env, generated bundles, DB secret files, or live profile state.
